cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "governance-research-regime: a logging protocol for developers who ship code they did not write"
message: "If you use this protocol, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Richard
    given-names: Holden
repository-code: "https://github.com/HoldenRichard/governance-research-regime"
abstract: >-
  A research instrument and engineering discipline for recording how a developer
  verifies, governs and remains accountable for a codebase authored largely by an
  AI agent. Comprises a session-log schema, an 18-column defect and near-miss
  ledger, an attestation register tracking formal platform and regulatory
  promises against ground truth, an identifier-discipline convention for
  multi-writer records, and a machine-checkable integrity gate. Contains the
  protocol only; no data.
keywords:
  - software engineering
  - AI-assisted development
  - agentic coding
  - research methods
  - governance
  - app store compliance
license: CC-BY-4.0
